Modifications made by StreamLine Labs, all of which are recorded in the
repository history and summarised here:

  * The `wincode` dependency requirement was changed from `>=0.4, <1` to the
    exact `=0.4.9`, so that a published consumer cannot resolve a second,
    semver-incompatible `wincode` on this edge. This is the reason the fork
    exists; see README.md.
  * The `bincode` 1.3.3 dev-dependency was removed (RUSTSEC-2025-0141) and the
    single test that used it now compares against hard-coded bincode 1.3.3
    output instead.
  * Package metadata (name, version, repository, authors) was updated to
    identify the fork.

The library source itself — `src/lib.rs`, `src/ser.rs`, `src/de.rs` — is
unmodified apart from a fork header comment and the test change noted above.

